==Strategy==
This stage's difficulty drops dramatically after getting [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], so, if you struggle or don't want want to risk wasting [[Cat Energy|energy]], get some/more of them before attempting this stage.

As long as you have all Anti-Starred Alien Treasures from at least one [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter, this stage should be quite straightforward. Use any [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] you have (Examples: [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] and [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress]]), along with a couple [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Aliens]], like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway]]. Just hold out with meatshields and your units should take care of the Aliens while your Critical Hitters take out the Metal Doges.

==Trivia==
*In real life, the [[wikipedia:Roswell UFO incident|Roswell UFO Incident]] was an incident in mid-1947 in which a "flying disc" crashed at a ranch near Roswell, New Mexico. This could be why the stage has [[Metal Doge]], who became a cyborg after an incident involving a silver disc in the sky.

